Ultrasonic Radar Scanner
An Arduino-based radar-style scanning system using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor mounted on a servo motor. The servo continuously scans from 0° to 100° while measuring the distance to objects.
Features
- Continuously scans an area using a servo motor
- Measures object distance using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor
- Displays distance in centimeters and inches on an LCD1602
- Green LED indicates the area is clear
- Red LED and buzzer activate when an object is detected within 15 cm
- Scanner stops at the detected object's position and resumes when the object moves away
Hardware
- Arduino Uno
- HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor
- SG90 Servo Motor
- LCD1602 Display
- Red LED
- Green LED
- Buzzer
- Breadboard and jumper wires
Key Concepts
- Ultrasonic distance measurement
- Servo motor control
- Sensor data processing
- LCD interfacing
- Conditional logic
- Real-time monitoring
- State-based scanning
